+**F9 — peak headroom is now effectively zero.** During the model-compliance-audit
+ballot the cgroup peaked at 98.2% of the 8 GiB cap with ~230 MB headroom, oscillating
+88–98% as seat processes start and finish. Zero OOM kills so far, but the margin that
+existed at the first sample (2.66 GiB) is gone: any all-seat sitting that overlaps with
+additional host load (an executive Kawun batch, a delegated worker wave) will produce
+the first OOM kill, terminating a seat mid-sitting. This is the concrete peak-side
+evidence for the Act 10 renewal debate: frequency savings are real (samples 4–5),
+peaks are not (samples 5–6). Ballot status: my yes is on branch
+`ballot/c1a00003-model-compliance-audit`, not yet merged to main by the clerk.
